# DiFede Games App - AI Development Rules

## Project Overview
DiFede Games (DiFedeAppV2) is a family game night score tracker built with Flask, PostgreSQL, Flask-SocketIO, and Bootstrap 5. It tracks scores for card and board games across multiple families with a crew/alliance system. It is NOT a rules engine -- it records scores only.

**Expert docs (read these first):**
- `APPLICATION_EXPERT_GUIDE.md` -- full architecture, all games, APIs, pitfalls (paste into new AI sessions)
- `CREATINGANEWGAME.MD` -- step-by-step new game checklist including image creation
- `README.md` -- service management, backup, troubleshooting

## Critical Rules

### Code Style
- NEVER use emojis in code, comments, templates, or UI text. No exceptions.
- NEVER add comments that just narrate what the code does. Comments should only explain non-obvious intent or trade-offs.
- Keep code clean, readable, and DRY. If you see duplication, refactor it.

### UX Philosophy
- **Common sense over cleverness.** The best interface is one nobody has to learn. If a user has to think about how something works, it's wrong.
- Labels must be clear and self-explanatory. Avoid jargon. "Who Wins?" beats "Scoring Direction".
- Mobile-first. Everything must look good and work perfectly on an iPhone.
- Match the active theme everywhere. No hardcoded colors - use CSS variables (--df-*).
- Every action should save immediately. Users should never lose data.

### Architecture
- PostgreSQL is the single source of truth. Scores save to DB on every entry.
- `game_scores` table is the unified score table for UNO games. `five_crowns_scores` is legacy (read-only fallback).
- The `/api/scores` endpoint handles all score persistence.
- Game types are defined in the `games` table. Adding a new game means: insert into `games`, create a template, add to SLUG_TO_URL mapping, add route alias, add dashboard slug cases (6 places). See CREATINGANEWGAME.MD.
- Family-based multi-tenancy: players belong to families, games belong to families, alliances connect families.

### Database
- V1 (difedeapp on port 5001) is the production database. V2 (difedeappv2 on port 5002) is the development database.
- ALWAYS back up the V2 database before making schema changes or data migrations.
- When syncing from V1, treat V1 data as sacred. Never modify V1.
- Use transactions for multi-step DB operations.

### Themes
- All themes are defined as CSS custom properties in base.html under [data-theme="..."] selectors.
- Key variables: --df-bg, --df-surface, --df-card, --df-text, --df-text-card, --df-accent, --df-accent-gradient, --df-border, --df-muted.
- NEVER use hardcoded colors in templates. Always reference --df-* variables.
- **CRITICAL: Light-on-light text bug.** Dark themes set body color to a LIGHT value (--df-text). Any element with a white/light background MUST explicitly set `color: #212529` or `color: var(--df-text-card)`. See `.cursor/rules/theme-text-contrast.mdc` for full details and protected classes.

### Testing Changes
- After code changes, kill ALL stale Python processes on port 5002 before restarting.
- Multiple processes on the same port = stale code being served. Always verify with `lsof -i :5002`.
- Clear browser cache aggressively when debugging visual issues.

### Server
- App runs on port 5002 via `python run.py` (binds to 0.0.0.0).
- Config is in config.py. DB credentials: user=difedeapp, password=Password, db=difedeappv2.
- Admin user: joe_71@yahoo.com (super_admin).

### File Structure
- Templates: app/templates/ (base.html, dashboard.html, five_crowns.html, uno_classic.html, gin_rummy.html, sevens.html, etc.)
- Routes: app/routes.py (main blueprint), app/auth_routes.py (auth blueprint)
- Config: config.py
- Entry point: run.py

### Quality Standards
- Enterprise-level thinking. Build it right, not fast.
- Handle edge cases. What happens with 0 players? 10 players? Empty data?
- Permission checks on every API endpoint. Family leads vs members vs super admin.
- Responsive design is not optional - it's required.
